item 1 measure has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 1 measure has the judgement "-The central database is implemented across several financial sectors (trading, post-trading, etc) in a consistent and coherent manner to ensure that the same digital solution can serve for the purpose of the documents/information storage and access across all relevant financial sectors.".

item 1 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeAlignmentMeasure".

item 1 measure has the description "Alignment with existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified".

item 1 measure has the title "MiFIR Central database".


item 2 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/2/measure".

item 2 measure is an assessment statement.

item 2 measure has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 2 measure has the judgement "-As the central database will be run by a European authority (ESMA), it will ensure that the data is submitted and accessed in a fair and non-disproportionate manner by all relevant authorities and market participants.".

item 2 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeOrganisationMeasure".

item 2 measure has the description "Organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services deliveryPlease list the governance measures foreseen".

item 2 measure has the title "MiFIR Central database".


item 3 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/3/measure".

item 3 measure is an assessment statement.

item 3 measure has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 3 measure has the judgement "-As the central database will be run by a European authority (ESMA), it will ensure that the data format is universally applied to all information/documents submitted by the relevant authorities and marker participants. Furthermore, the information to be submitted (notably for authorisations) is set out in legislation.".

item 3 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeSharedMeasure".

item 3 measure has the description "Measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the dataPlease list such measures".

item 3 measure has the title "MiFIR Central database".


item 4 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/4/measure".

item 4 measure is an assessment statement.

item 4 measure has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 4 measure has the judgement "-As the central database will be run by a European authority (ESMA), it will ensure that the data format is universally applied to all information/documents submitted by the relevant authorities and marker participants. Furthermore, the information to be submitted (notably for authorisations) is set out in legislation.".

item 4 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeStandardsMeasure".

item 4 measure has the description "Use of commonly agreed open technical specifications and standardsPlease list such measures".

item 4 measure has the title "MiFIR Central database".


